{"lines":[{"x":0.081314881021614036,"h":0.0176066371258361,"w":0.20069203694661458,"t":"Sample Writing answers","y":0.060881735232486078,"c":1},{"y":0.10901162788451302,"w":0.30622838338216146,"t":"TEST 4, WRITING TASK 2","h":0.021849113715287305,"c":1,"x":0.079584770171150107},{"h":0.020303772912315776,"y":0.14491671978306253,"c":1,"x":0.081239214801941184,"t":"This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 7.5 score.","w":0.60048294067382812},{"x":0.081260767606803105,"y":0.17400046618365173,"t":"Nowadays individuals are arguing that primary schools pay a lot of attention to the","w":0.68350051879882812,"h":0.02002232019679373,"c":1},{"w":0.68512110392252601,"h":0.01896451385476694,"c":1,"t":"formal methods of learning. I partially agree with this point of view, however I think","x":0.081314880501826212,"y":0.19622093026056087},{"c":1,"y":0.216304034016641,"x":0.081238082782356433,"w":0.54337732950846362,"t":"play is extremely crucial in the classroom full of primary students.","h":0.020732690105077833},{"c":1,"t":"To begin with, formal learning plays an important role, since it teaches the student","h":0.02185503864221594,"x":0.08123688897215374,"y":0.24464036909651188,"w":0.67837163289388014},{"y":0.26629913201121314,"x":0.081255879162447406,"h":0.020332927049833027,"c":1,"t":"about being disciplined and respectful to everyone. Discipline and respect are two","w":0.66794062296549483},{"h":0.021482918794710648,"y":0.28752584705058792,"w":0.67490341186523439,"x":0.081247225787505789,"c":1,"t":"most important skills we need in our life that schools teaches us in a way of formal"},{"y":0.30854256820287829,"t":"learning. Getting into details, these skills make people succeed in their lives. If we look","w":0.69912475585937495,"c":1,"h":0.020864034883620541,"x":0.081244917079132228},{"c":1,"w":0.71799306233723958,"x":0.08131488743833766,"t":"at the example of successfull people today they all have these two qualities in common.","y":0.33135059460115501,"h":0.017494751574527734},{"w":0.7231833902994792,"y":0.35164450643831391,"h":0.017541540344750861,"c":1,"x":0.083044983120156526,"t":"Moreover formal learning helps us to test the ability of a student by conducting an exam"},{"y":0.37194603105995472,"x":0.079550059570464571,"t":"in a formal way, which shows us how much has a student learnt and how much is the","w":0.69904703776041666,"h":0.020823419970011248,"c":1},{"y":0.39401135906155438,"x":0.081097962702471882,"t":"student capable of doing.","h":0.020072471186195484,"w":0.21142457326253256,"c":1},{"w":0.69559417724609374,"t":"On the other hand, I believe that too formal education is not the best way of learning.","x":0.082991868160814691,"h":0.020400609896681909,"c":1,"y":0.42188924466794087},{"w":0.69550170898437502,"h":0.01894620584390494,"t":"Considering the stage of the life in which primary students belong, we need to realize","y":0.44471658482012644,"x":0.083044993176223533,"c":1},{"w":0.70605367024739585,"c":1,"x":0.082963230010913755,"y":0.46360106536051326,"t":"that fun is a crucial part of it. Being extremely formal blocks that fun from a student's","h":0.021701533782724103},{"c":1,"w":0.65224914550781254,"x":0.08304497735480193,"t":"life. So instead of schools being strict about formal ways of learning they should","y":0.48691860436889089,"h":0.01744186102384615},{"y":0.50726744188343065,"t":"promote fun methods of teaching. For example, mind games other other video games,","h":0.018974685268522307,"x":0.083044985034958732,"w":0.70069203694661464,"c":1},{"t":"colours, paints and other activities will also teach student but in a enjoyable way. These","x":0.08295890974784878,"y":0.52726920128901966,"w":0.71471435546874995,"h":0.022456061681556561,"c":1},{"w":0.70080200195312503,"x":0.08299488063558802,"t":"activities will also promote the important skills such as social skills, creative skills and","y":0.54938869244601951,"c":1,"h":0.020284664722653556},{"y":0.56969552437791404,"c":1,"t":"other beneficial skills we need in our daily lives. Furthermore, if we consider it deeply it","x":0.082967637723101575,"w":0.71125630696614583,"h":0.022500093538832866},{"w":0.69731480916341149,"c":1,"t":"will also prevent boredom and will motivate the student to have a passion for lifelong","y":0.59136100477003439,"x":0.083001029869290907,"h":0.019296508639571219},{"h":0.023791255110039322,"t":"learning. last but not the least, play in the primary classroom has a huge importance on","x":0.082949225654837158,"w":0.72164983113606762,"c":1,"y":0.61126478757891944},{"t":"it's own. which gives the student this freedom to enjoy learning.","x":0.083045005024656143,"y":0.6336599022594851,"h":0.01895637659028826,"w":0.52076121012369792,"c":1},{"h":0.019564017955868152,"c":1,"w":0.69731684366861979,"t":"In conclusion, formal learning has it's importance till some extent but sometimes it is","x":0.082992939167003496,"y":0.66274619420122693},{"h":0.022374532871766828,"w":0.68023096720377607,"t":"a necessity to be informal. And schools should be focused at both of the methods of","x":0.08462915768038641,"c":1,"y":0.68179040053199691},{"t":"learning","x":0.082628687351535932,"h":0.017051783535679044,"c":1,"y":0.70692325888298424,"w":0.071938966115315764},{"c":1,"t":"Here is the examiner's comment:","h":0.015988371937820545,"y":0.74273255801728144,"w":0.27162628173828124,"x":0.0847750952684026},{"y":0.76452064372160666,"w":0.65397923787434897,"c":1,"t":"This is an excellent response that presents a range of relevant ideas. The writer","h":0.017494751574527623,"x":0.12456747457948912},{"w":0.64013839721679688,"x":0.12456747952089245,"y":0.7834149757992338,"t":"sets out their position in the opening paragraph, and addresses both parts of","h":0.018910605562075355,"c":1},{"x":0.12445958159676877,"h":0.022114360641148467,"w":0.66456542968749999,"c":1,"y":0.7993336313784396,"t":"the question. Paragraph 2 presents the importance of formal learning: it teaches"},{"y":0.81976744157761183,"c":1,"t":"discipline and respect, it allows people to take exams to show how much they","h":0.017531368930995495,"x":0.12456747126688318,"w":0.6453287251790365},{"y":0.83676222025098124,"h":0.021155111768013768,"w":0.67144480387369787,"c":1,"t":"have learned and are capable of. Paragraph 3 goes on to present the importance","x":0.12448967584317046},{"x":0.1244654241395267,"h":0.022614780049627581,"c":1,"y":0.85404881924955356,"w":0.64729395548502611,"t":"of play: being too formal blocks fun, schools should promote 'fun' methods of"},{"w":0.65418340047200518,"t":"teaching, they make suggestions of types of games and activities that could be","h":0.022242811695523335,"c":1,"x":0.12446169431483677,"y":0.87287520716837852},{"y":0.89230859114500316,"x":0.12624659280144651,"h":0.02012515151475669,"t":"used to teach in an enjoyable way, prevent boredom, and instil a love for lifelong","c":1,"w":0.6679203796386719},{"t":"learning. The conclusion brings the response to an end, but is quite general. It is","x":0.12448015409348329,"y":0.90980132570274042,"c":1,"w":0.66626907348632813,"h":0.022627772444023586},{"c":1,"w":0.34135233561197914,"h":0.026604721144081522,"x":0.12423735043889754,"t":"appropriate, but could be more focused.","y":0.92594311660913375},{"w":0.032871971130371103,"h":0.01308139510051276,"y":0.95930232566708296,"c":1,"t":"138","x":0.084775087012669129}],"w":2400,"h":2857}